  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset landscape in late 2026 is defined by a deep-seated structural realignment as the CLARITY Act nears crucial Senate floor action. This regulatory shift is having direct ramifications across the BTC/ETH divide. While institutional demand for spot Bitcoin ETFs has hit a notable plateau\u2014witnessing its first calendar year of net outflows and key corporate balance sheet liquidations\u2014it remains a highly consolidated institutional asset class. Concurrently, the emerging regulatory framework is catalyzing the development of Bitcoin-native programmability, directly challenging Ethereum's long-standing smart contract monopoly. Finally, the critical vulnerability of historical multi-chain bridges is driving rapid technical evolution in non-custodial, trust-minimized cross-chain liquidity networks to connect BTC and EVM execution environments seamlessly.",
